  VALUE: DEC-EXECUTABLE-RULES-ROADMAP
  ROLE: Governed_By
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SPIKE-EXECUTABLE-RULES
  ROLE: Proven_By

[SLICE]
UID: SLICE-GRAMMAR-FROM-NIX
TITLE: Generate the grammar from a typed Nix option surface, and gate it
DEPTH: needs-design
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Define the grammar as a typed Nix option tree, with every shared field
declared once and each node type selecting the fields it carries (STATUS
differs between DECISION and SPIKE, so a type may specialise a field).
Relations and prefixes per type; no untyped option anywhere. Generate
docs/sdoc/grammar.sgra from it, byte-identical to today's, together with a
committed record of which fields count as a node's contract; keep the @repo
alias resolving. Commit the generated files and add a drift check, so a stale
grammar is a red check. Add the validation gate: a clean-directory strictdoc
export over the whole corpus at commit time and in CI, because some grammar
defects only surface through documents.

Consumer surface the operator reviews before implementation: the option tree
for node types and fields, with one question decided there first -- whether
field order is one global list or per node type (strictdoc accepts both).
Reviewed after: the regenerated grammar as an empty diff, and the gate firing
on a deliberately broken fixture.

Not included: behaviour, transitions, ownership rules, and which fields count
as contract -- this delivers the surface, not the values.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Proven in the spike: a typed surface regenerates the grammar byte-for-byte in
0.03 s and rejects thirteen of thirteen bad declarations once the merged value
is forced, and strictdoc rejects six of six injected grammar defects. The gate
needs nothing but the strictdoc package. Two rules carried from the
measurement: cross-field checks live in one place that forces evaluation of
the whole value, because Nix's addCheck never runs on a nested option; and the
corpus export is the second gate.
<<<
PARENT_FP: >>>
DEC-EXECUTABLE-RULES-ROADMAP:0000000
DEC-FP-FIELDS-CONFIGURABLE:0000000
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Carry the rest of strictdoc's native grammar features rather than excluding
them as design choices: human-readable field titles, composite nodes, view
styles, child relations, file roles, and an explicit no-prefix option. Update
the sdoc skill wherever the generated grammar changes its instructions.
<<<
