[SLICE]
UID: SLICE-SDOC-CLI
TITLE: A command-line tool that is the only writer of sdoc files
DEPTH: needs-design
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Build the tool through which every node is created and changed: create, set,
relate and move, with flags derived from the generated grammar (fields,
choices, relation roles); UIDs minted through strictdoc's own hook; required
fields filled from arguments so a TBD never lands; every write validated
against the whole graph as it would be after the write, before the file is
replaced; formatting applied by the same code path. Deny direct edits of sdoc
and grammar files in the agent harness, before the edit tool runs, and point
the model at the tool. No lifecycle verbs yet: this milestone is create, read,
update and delete.

Consumer surface the operator reviews before implementation: the verb list
and their flags. Reviewed after: a session that authors nodes through the
tool only, and a direct edit being refused.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
In the operator's words, the root failure is a model producing incorrect
formats with nothing validating the write; the tool takes the model's hands
off the files. Measured: creating a node in-process costs 0.35 s, validating
the whole graph 0.3 s, and strictdoc's node model writes any field in grammar
order -- nothing here waits on the behaviour model.
<<<
PARENT_FP: DEC-EXECUTABLE-RULES-ROADMAP:0000000
NOTES: >>>
Build on strictdoc's own machinery rather than re-implementing writes: manage
new for scaffolding, set_field_value for fields, the writer for formatting.
The cache directory must live outside the checkout for worktrees. Validating
the whole graph per command costs about a second on this corpus and about
two at five thousand nodes when strictdoc's cache is warm, which needs the
working copy at a stable path; a fresh temporary copy pays the cold cost.
<<<
