[SLICE]
UID: SLICE-INSTANCE-SEMANTICS-MIGRATION
TITLE: Migrate this system's own semantics onto the plumbing
DEPTH: needs-design
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Express this system's own semantics in the behaviour model and retire the
hand-written scripts they live in today: which fields count as a node's
contract; a signed edge as evidence that goes stale when the parent's
contract changes; readiness -- everything a node depends on is settled -- and
its count of open decisions as gates; signing and the authorship flip as moves
with a rule about who may make them; revocation made visible. The two keys
stay separate: an independent session marks a node verified, and only the
operator claims authorship. The decisions this milestone needs are the
instance's own -- who may sign, whether DEPTH may move backwards, whether
implemented and verified belong in DEPTH, agent identity -- and are taken at
its review, not before.

Consumer surface the operator reviews before implementation: the instance's
lifecycle rendered from the model, with those decisions marked. Reviewed
after: the existing fingerprint and readiness checks pass through the new
validators with identical results on the real graph.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Migration last keeps the open instance decisions from blocking the plumbing,
and the plumbing is what makes those decisions reviewable rather than guessed.
<<<
PARENT_FP: >>>
DEC-EXECUTABLE-RULES-ROADMAP:0000000
DEC-FINGERPRINT-IN-NODE:0000000
DEC-FP-ACCEPT-AUTHORITY:0000000
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Git-flow handling -- rebase, squash lineage, pre-merge collection -- stays
deferred until a branch reaches main, per MECH-FP-GIT-FLOW-HAZARDS.
<<<
